<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Ethics Statement</h2>

<div id="Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">TROLL improves the efficiency of LLM finetuning by enabling scalable trust-region optimization.
While our experiments focus on mathematical reasoning, the method is broadly applicable to other domains.
As with any advance in LLM training, this carries both potential benefits and risks, depending on the context of deployment.
We believe that managing and shaping the societal impacts of increasingly powerful LLMs should not be left to individual researchers, organizations, or companies alone, but they must be carefully governed and regulated by sovereign governments and strong democratic institutions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Reproducibility Statement</h2>

<div id="Ax2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments in this paper rely on publicly available pretrained checkpoints.
We exclusively use publicly available datasets.
While some were modified, we describe these modifications and will release the processed versions upon the deanonymization of the paper.
Further information, together with additional hyperparameters and training details, are provided in <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Experimental Setup ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix C</span></a>.
Our implementation builds on open-source repositories and will be made available after deanonymization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">On LLM Usage</h2>

<div id="Ax3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used LLMs to assist with revising grammar, style, and text flow in this manuscript.
In addition, we employed LLMs to support aspects of the implementation and generate visualizations for this manuscript.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Derivations</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each output token <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> the trust region projection layer solves</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\underset{\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\arg\min}\textrm{KL}\left({\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\parallel{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">o</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒒</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.710em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underset{\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\arg\min}\textrm{KL}\left({\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\parallel{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">s.t.</span>  </td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\parallel{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\right)&lt;\epsilon~~\text{and}~~\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\right]=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>and</mtext><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\parallel{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\right)&lt;\epsilon~~\text{and}~~\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\right]=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, the first constraint enforces the trust region to the previous distribution <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> and the second constraint ensures the resulting distribution is properly normalized.
We solve the constrained optimization problem using the method of Lagrangian multipliers and start with the primal solution.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Primal Solution</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To compute the primal solution of this optimization problem, we first set up the Lagrangian function by introducing Lagrangian multipliers <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for the first and second constraint, respectively.
The corresponding Lagrangian is given as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}),\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}),\eta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\parallel{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\right)-\eta(\epsilon-\textrm{KL}\left({\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\parallel{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\parallel{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\right)-\eta(\epsilon-\textrm{KL}\left({\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\parallel{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\lambda\left(1-\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\lambda\left(1-\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-(\eta\epsilon+\lambda)+\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\left(\log\dfrac{\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}+\eta\log\dfrac{\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}+\lambda\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-(\eta\epsilon+\lambda)+\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\left(\log\dfrac{\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}+\eta\log\dfrac{\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}+\lambda\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-(\eta\epsilon+\lambda)+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-(\eta\epsilon+\lambda)+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{o_{t}}\bigl[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\bigl((\eta+1)\log\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})(\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}))+\lambda\bigr)\bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{o_{t}}\bigl[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\bigl((\eta+1)\log\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})(\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}))+\lambda\bigr)\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We can now obtain the optimal primal solution to <a href="#A1.E7" title="7 ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 7</span></a> by taking the derivative of the Lagrangian w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>, setting it to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and solving for <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The derivative is given by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}(\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}),\eta)}{\partial\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}(\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}),\eta)}{\partial\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{o}\left[(\eta+1)+(\eta+1)\log\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})-(\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}))+\lambda\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>o</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{o}\left[(\eta+1)+(\eta+1)\log\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})-(\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}))+\lambda\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Clearly <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nicefrac{{\partial\mathcal{L}(\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}),\eta)}}{{\partial\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">o</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒒</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.710em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">η</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">o</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒒</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.710em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nicefrac{{\partial\mathcal{L}(\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}),\eta)}}{{\partial\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> if all the individual terms of the sum are <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the problem simplifies to</p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0=(\eta+1)+(\eta+1)\log\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})-(\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}))+\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0=(\eta+1)+(\eta+1)\log\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})-(\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}))+\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which yields</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})=\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}))-(\eta+1+\lambda)}{\eta+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})=\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t}))-(\eta+1+\lambda)}{\eta+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">and thus</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)\exp\left(-\dfrac{\eta+1+\lambda}{\eta+1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)\exp\left(-\dfrac{\eta+1+\lambda}{\eta+1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\propto\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\propto\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Crucially, this primal solution allows computing a properly normalized distribution <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> without explicitly computing <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> by replacing the <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>exp</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#A1.E10" title="10 ‣ A.1 Primal Solution ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 10</span></a> with a softmax.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Dual Solution</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The second step of the Lagrangian multiplier method is to solve the dual problem which finds the optimal dual parameters given the primal solution.
To that end, we insert the primal solution from <a href="#A1.E9" title="9 ‣ A.1 Primal Solution ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 9</span></a> into the Lagrangian (<a href="#A1.E8" title="8 ‣ A.1 Primal Solution ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 8</span></a>). Here most terms cancel out, leading to a dual of the form</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(\eta,\lambda)=-\eta\epsilon-\lambda-\eta-1=-\eta\epsilon-(\eta+1+\lambda)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(\eta,\lambda)=-\eta\epsilon-\lambda-\eta-1=-\eta\epsilon-(\eta+1+\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In a second step towards a practically usable dual, we remove the dependency on <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> by exploiting the constraint it enforces, i.e., <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\right]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\right]=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Going to log space and again using <a href="#A1.E9" title="9 ‣ A.1 Primal Solution ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 9</span></a>, this property yields</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)\exp\left(-\dfrac{\eta+1+\lambda}{\eta+1}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)\exp\left(-\dfrac{\eta+1+\lambda}{\eta+1}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\dfrac{\eta+1+\lambda}{\eta+1}+\log\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\dfrac{\eta+1+\lambda}{\eta+1}+\log\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which we can rewrite as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta+1+\lambda=(\eta+1)\log\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta+1+\lambda=(\eta+1)\log\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Now, inserting <a href="#A1.E12" title="12 ‣ A.2 Dual Solution ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 12</span></a> into <a href="#A1.E11" title="11 ‣ A.2 Dual Solution ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 11</span></a> removes the dependency on <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> leading to</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(\eta)=-\eta\epsilon-(\eta+1)\log\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(\eta)=-\eta\epsilon-(\eta+1)\log\sum_{o_{t}}\left[\exp\left(\dfrac{\log\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})+\eta\log{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\eta+1}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Using this dual, we can find the optimal <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> by solving</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta^{*}=\arg\max_{\eta}d(\eta)~~s.t.~~\eta\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>η</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.827em">.</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta^{*}=\arg\max_{\eta}d(\eta)~~s.t.~~\eta\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">We can efficiently optimize this scalar optimization problem using the <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-ary bracketing method described in <a href="#LST3" title="Listing 3 ‣ Appendix B Code ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Gradients</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This trust region projection is trivially differentiable using standard autograd tools, except for the numerical optimization of the dual to find the optimal step size <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Towards differentiating through this optimization problem in closed form, let us first change perspective and no longer consider the distributions <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> directly but vectors <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the probabilities of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}</annotation></semantics></math> denote to the normalized logits of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We further assume all <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> vectors are normalized, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum q=1,~~\sum\exp{{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}}=1~~,\textrm{and}\sum\exp{\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.660em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum q=1,~~\sum\exp{{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}}=1~~,\textrm{and}\sum\exp{\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">While this notation may seem slightly unintuitive at first, it simplifies the following derivations.
As we assume the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> and consequently <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}</annotation></semantics></math> are constant, the only gradient we are interested in is <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dfrac{\partial\eta^{*}}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dfrac{\partial\eta^{*}}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., how the output of the original LLM’s output influences the optimal step size <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since we do not have an analytical form for the optimal step size <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> but only the result of the numerical optimization, we need to introduce further analytical properties.
Using the implicit differentiation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dontchev &amp; Rockafellar, 2009</a>)</cite> and differentiable matrix calculus techniques <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Magnus &amp; Neudecker, 1989</a>)</cite> techniques introduced to deep learning by OptNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Amos &amp; Kolter, 2017</a>)</cite>, we start by writing out the Karush–Kuhn–Tucker (KKT) conditions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karush, 1939</a>)</cite> of the dual <a href="#A1.E13" title="13 ‣ A.2 Dual Solution ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 13</span></a> for the optimum at <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denoting the Lagrangian multiplier corresponding to the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> constraint by <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and realizing that <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla d(\eta)=\epsilon-\textrm{KL}\left({\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\parallel{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\right)={\epsilon}-q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla d(\eta)=\epsilon-\textrm{KL}\left({\pi(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\parallel{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\right)={\epsilon}-q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})</annotation></semantics></math>, those are given by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{\nabla g(\eta^{*})+\mu\nabla(-\eta^{*})=\epsilon-q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}))+\mu=0}_{\textrm{Stationarity}}~~~~~~\text{and}~~\underbrace{\mu(-\eta^{*})=0}_{\textrm{Complementary Slackness}}\!\!." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>old</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Stationarity</mtext></munder><mspace style="width:1.98em;" width="1.98em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Complementary Slackness</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{\nabla g(\eta^{*})+\mu\nabla(-\eta^{*})=\epsilon-q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}))+\mu=0}_{\textrm{Stationarity}}~~~~~~\text{and}~~\underbrace{\mu(-\eta^{*})=0}_{\textrm{Complementary Slackness}}\!\!.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">As there is no equality constraint in <a href="#A1.E13" title="13 ‣ A.2 Dual Solution ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 13</span></a>, primal feasibility is given by default.
We can now take the total differentials around these conditions, which are given by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d\left(\epsilon-q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})+\mu\right)=-d\left(q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})\right)-d\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d\left(\epsilon-q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})+\mu\right)=-d\left(q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})\right)-d\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d(\mu(-\eta^{*})=d\mu(-\eta^{*})+\mu(-d\eta^{*})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d(\mu(-\eta^{*})=d\mu(-\eta^{*})+\mu(-d\eta^{*}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes as it is constant.
Before proceeding, we need to rewrite the KL term <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\left(q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\left(q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})\right)</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}</annotation></semantics></math> and simplify.
First, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d\left(q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})\right)=(1+\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})^{T}dq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d\left(q^{T}(\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})\right)=(1+\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})^{T}dq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and need to continue with the differential <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dq</annotation></semantics></math>.
Again using the primal solution <a href="#A1.E10" title="10 ‣ A.1 Primal Solution ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 10</span></a>, we get</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q=\textrm{softmax}\left(\dfrac{\eta^{*}{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}+\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}{\eta^{*}+1}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q=\textrm{softmax}\left(\dfrac{\eta^{*}{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}+\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}{\eta^{*}+1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Assuming the old logits are a constant, we can write the corresponding differential as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle dq=\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}d\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}+\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\eta^{*}}d\eta^{*}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle dq=\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}d\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}+\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\eta^{*}}d\eta^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Inserting this term into <a href="#A1.E16" title="16 ‣ A.3 Gradients ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 16</span></a> and the plugging the result into <a href="#A1.E14" title="14 ‣ A.3 Gradients ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 14</span></a> yields</p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\left(1+\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}\right)^{T}\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\eta^{*}}d\eta^{*}-d\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\left(1+\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}\right)^{T}\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\eta^{*}}d\eta^{*}-d\mu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1+\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}\right)\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}d\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1+\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}\right)\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}d\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\mu d\eta^{*}-\eta^{*}d\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\mu d\eta^{*}-\eta^{*}d\mu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.8" class="ltx_p">which we can use to compute the desired gradient <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dfrac{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}{\partial\eta^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dfrac{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}{\partial\eta^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To this end, we consider <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> separate cases.
First, if the original KL trust region is not violated, then <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{*}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{*}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, <a href="#A1.E19" title="19 ‣ A.3 Gradients ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 19</span></a> directly yields that <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\eta^{*}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\eta^{*}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and thus the entire gradient <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dfrac{\partial\eta^{*}}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dfrac{\partial\eta^{*}}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}</annotation></semantics></math> is zero.
Second, the original KL trust region constraint is active and thus <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{*}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{*}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case <a href="#A1.E19" title="19 ‣ A.3 Gradients ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 19</span></a> gives <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math> which simplifies <a href="#A1.E18" title="18 ‣ A.3 Gradients ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 18</span></a>. Reordering the remaining terms gives the required gradient</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\eta^{*}}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}=\dfrac{1}{-(1+\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})^{T}\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\eta^{*}}}(1+\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})^{T}\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\eta^{*}}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}=\dfrac{1}{-(1+\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})^{T}\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\eta^{*}}}(1+\log q-{q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})})^{T}\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.9" class="ltx_p">The required partial derivatives can be obtained from <a href="#A1.E17" title="17 ‣ A.3 Gradients ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 17</span></a></p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}=\frac{1}{\eta^{*}+1}(\textrm{D}(q)-qq^{T})\quad\text{and}\quad\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\eta^{*}}=\frac{1}{(\eta+1)^{2}}(\textrm{D}(q)-qq^{T})({q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}-\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>D</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>D</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>log</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}}=\frac{1}{\eta^{*}+1}(\textrm{D}(q)-qq^{T})\quad\text{and}\quad\dfrac{\partial q}{\partial\eta^{*}}=\frac{1}{(\eta+1)^{2}}(\textrm{D}(q)-qq^{T})({q}_{\textrm{old}}^{(\textrm{log})}-\tilde{q}^{(\textrm{log})}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.10" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(q)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a diagonal matrix with the entries of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> on the diagonal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Crucially, for practical purposes, we never need to explicitly materialize the matrices in the partial derivatives.
The resulting backward introduces negligible computational and memory overhead and, in the non-sparsified case, can be written in less than 10 lines of python code.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Sparsification</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any pair of logits <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\geq\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\geq\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> w.l.o.g., the logit-wise terms that sum to the KL are equally ordered</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\quad\geq\quad\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo>≥</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}\quad\geq\quad\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\log\frac{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">iff <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\kappa}\geq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>κ</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\kappa}\geq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=\frac{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\frac{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}</annotation></semantics></math> is the current probability ratio of the pair and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}=\gamma\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}{{\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})}=\gamma\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> gives the multiplier of the old ratio.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Rewrite <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\geq\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(1)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})\geq\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(2)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x_{1})=\kappa\cdot p(x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x_{1})=\kappa\cdot p(x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x_{i})=\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(i)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x_{i})=\tilde{\pi}(o_{t}^{(i)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> for clarity and similarly replace <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(x_{i})={\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}^{(i)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(x_{i})={\pi}_{\textrm{old}}(o_{t}^{(i)}\,|\,\bm{q},\bm{o}_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then compare the contributions of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to the KL divergence</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\kappa p(x_{2})\log\frac{\kappa p(x_{2})}{q(x_{1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\kappa p(x_{2})\log\frac{\kappa p(x_{2})}{q(x_{1})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq p(x_{2})\log\frac{p(x_{2})}{q(x_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq p(x_{2})\log\frac{p(x_{2})}{q(x_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\kappa\log k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\kappa\log k</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\log\frac{q(x_{1})}{q(x_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\log\frac{q(x_{1})}{q(x_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody><tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left" style="white-space:normal;" colspan="5">and substitute <math id="A1.EGx25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{q(x_{1})}{q(x_{2})}\eqcolon\gamma\frac{p(x_{1})}{p(x_{2})}=\gamma\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{q(x_{1})}{q(x_{2})}\eqcolon\gamma\frac{p(x_{1})}{p(x_{2})}=\gamma\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e^{\kappa}\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>κ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e^{\kappa}\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\gamma\frac{p(x_{1})}{p(x_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\gamma\frac{p(x_{1})}{p(x_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e^{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>κ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e^{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\gamma." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\gamma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here, the assumption that the relative likelihood <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> was not exponentially larger before usually holds in practice, as the token distributions are pushed farther from uniform during training <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cui et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any subset <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of the possible tokens, we define <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, or just <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> when the mask is clear, as the <em id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sparsed</em> distribution.
For tokens not in <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, it has default probability <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and the same probability as <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> for all others up to the renormalization constant.</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{S}}(x)=p^{\prime}(x)\coloneq\begin{cases}\gamma p(x),&amp;\mathrm{for}~x\in\mathcal{S}\\
p_{d},&amp;\mathrm{else}\end{cases},\qquad\gamma=\frac{1-(|\mathcal{V}|-|\mathcal{S}|)\cdot p_{d}}{\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}p(x)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>else</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{S}}(x)=p^{\prime}(x)\coloneq\begin{cases}\gamma p(x),&amp;\mathrm{for}~x\in\mathcal{S}\\
p_{d},&amp;\mathrm{else}\end{cases},\qquad\gamma=\frac{1-(|\mathcal{V}|-|\mathcal{S}|)\cdot p_{d}}{\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}p(x)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The renormalization factor <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> accounts for the previous total mass <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}p(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}p(x)</annotation></semantics></math> of the kept tokens and new mass <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(|\mathcal{V}|-|\mathcal{S}|)\cdot p_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(|\mathcal{V}|-|\mathcal{S}|)\cdot p_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of the dropped tokens.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In the case of equal sparsification masks for distributions <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math>, we can prove a practically tight upper bound for the true divergence <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the sparse divergence <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given categorical distributions <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math> over the vocabulary <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math> with identical top-<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> logits, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{topk(p)}=\operatorname{topk(q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>topk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>topk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{topk(p)}=\operatorname{topk(q)}</annotation></semantics></math>, of equal total probability <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{x\in\operatorname{topk(p)}}p(x)=\sum_{x\in\operatorname{topk(q)}}q(x)=1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>topk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>topk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{x\in\operatorname{topk(p)}}p(x)=\sum_{x\in\operatorname{topk(q)}}q(x)=1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the sparsed distributions <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime},q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime},q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with density</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}(x)\coloneq\begin{cases}\gamma p(x),&amp;\mathrm{for}~x\in\operatorname{topk(p)}\\
p_{d},&amp;\mathrm{else}\end{cases},\quad q^{\prime}(x_{i})\coloneq\begin{cases}\gamma q(x),&amp;\mathrm{for}~x\in\operatorname{topk(q)}\\
p_{d},&amp;\mathrm{else}\end{cases}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>topk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>else</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>topk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>else</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}(x)\coloneq\begin{cases}\gamma p(x),&amp;\mathrm{for}~x\in\operatorname{topk(p)}\\
p_{d},&amp;\mathrm{else}\end{cases},\quad q^{\prime}(x_{i})\coloneq\begin{cases}\gamma q(x),&amp;\mathrm{for}~x\in\operatorname{topk(q)}\\
p_{d},&amp;\mathrm{else}\end{cases},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and normalization constant <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(\delta,k,|\mathcal{V}|,p_{d})\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(\delta,k,|\mathcal{V}|,p_{d})\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math> follow the inequality</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)\leq\gamma^{-1}\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)\leq\gamma^{-1}\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\min}=\arg\min_{x}q(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\min}=\arg\min_{x}q(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Rename the logits in descending order of probability under p, such that <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x_{0})\geq p(x_{1})\geq\cdots\geq p(x_{|\mathcal{V}|-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x_{0})\geq p(x_{1})\geq\cdots\geq p(x_{|\mathcal{V}|-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume there is <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math> such that the largest <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> logits of both <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> have exactly the total probability mass <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=0}^{k}p(x_{i})=\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}q(x_{i})=1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=0}^{k}p(x_{i})=\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}q(x_{i})=1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and the subset of largest logits is identical.
Every nondegenerate distribution has <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\min}\leq q(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\min}\leq q(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x_{i})\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x_{i})\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>, as the total mass could otherwise not be <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
So split the sum over logits in the KL divergence and apply both inequalities</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}p(x_{i})\log\frac{p(x_{i})}{q(x_{i})}+\sum_{i=k}^{|\mathcal{V}|-1}p(x_{i})\log\frac{p(x_{i})}{q(x_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}p(x_{i})\log\frac{p(x_{i})}{q(x_{i})}+\sum_{i=k}^{|\mathcal{V}|-1}p(x_{i})\log\frac{p(x_{i})}{q(x_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
