<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}p(x_{i})\log\frac{p(x_{i})}{q(x_{i})}+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}p(x_{i})\log\frac{p(x_{i})}{q(x_{i})}+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Replace p, and analogously q, with their sparsed version as defined in <a href="#A1.Thmdefinition1" title="Definition A.1. ‣ A.4 Sparsification ‣ Appendix A Derivations ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition A.1</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}(x_{i})\coloneq\begin{cases}\gamma p(x_{i}),&amp;\mathrm{for}~i&lt;k\\
p_{d},&amp;\mathrm{for}~i\geq k\end{cases}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}(x_{i})\coloneq\begin{cases}\gamma p(x_{i}),&amp;\mathrm{for}~i&lt;k\\
p_{d},&amp;\mathrm{for}~i\geq k\end{cases},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{1-(|\mathcal{V}|-k)\cdot p_{d}}{(1-\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{1-(|\mathcal{V}|-k)\cdot p_{d}}{(1-\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math> renormalizes the <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> mass of the selected tokens to account for the default mass <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(|\mathcal{V}|-k)\cdot p_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(|\mathcal{V}|-k)\cdot p_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of the sparsified tokens.
Multiplying with ones and adding a zero to the KL bound yields the relation to the sparse KL,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}\frac{\gamma}{\gamma}p(x_{i})\log\frac{\gamma p(x_{i})}{\gamma q(x_{i})}+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}}+\gamma^{-1}\sum_{i=k}^{|\mathcal{V}|-1}p^{\prime}(x_{i})\underbrace{\log\frac{p_{d}}{p_{d}}}_{=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}\frac{\gamma}{\gamma}p(x_{i})\log\frac{\gamma p(x_{i})}{\gamma q(x_{i})}+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}}+\gamma^{-1}\sum_{i=k}^{|\mathcal{V}|-1}p^{\prime}(x_{i})\underbrace{\log\frac{p_{d}}{p_{d}}}_{=0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\gamma^{-1}\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}p^{\prime}(x_{i})\log\frac{p^{\prime}(x_{i})}{q^{\prime}(x_{i})}+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}}+\gamma^{-1}\sum_{i=k}^{|\mathcal{V}|-1}p^{\prime}(x_{i})\log\frac{p^{\prime}(x_{i})}{q^{\prime}(x_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\gamma^{-1}\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}p^{\prime}(x_{i})\log\frac{p^{\prime}(x_{i})}{q^{\prime}(x_{i})}+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}}+\gamma^{-1}\sum_{i=k}^{|\mathcal{V}|-1}p^{\prime}(x_{i})\log\frac{p^{\prime}(x_{i})}{q^{\prime}(x_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\gamma^{-1}\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\gamma^{-1}\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Assuming that <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>’s probabilities can be represented by normal single precision IEEE-754 numbers, <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\min}&gt;1.17549\cdot 10^{-38}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1.17549</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>38</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\min}&gt;1.17549\cdot 10^{-38}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\ll|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\ll|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math>, e.g. <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=256</annotation></semantics></math> of vocab size <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}|=151936" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>151936</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}|=151936</annotation></semantics></math> while using threshold <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> and default mass <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{d}=10^{-12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{d}=10^{-12}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sparse KL approximation,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{(1-\delta)}{1-(|\mathcal{V}|-k)\cdot p_{d}}\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{(1-\delta)}{1-(|\mathcal{V}|-k)\cdot p_{d}}\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+\delta\log\frac{\delta}{q_{\min}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{0.99999}{1-151680\cdot 10^{-12}}\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+10^{-5}\log\frac{10^{-5}}{1.17549\cdot 10^{-38}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>0.99999</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>151680</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>1.17549</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>38</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{0.99999}{1-151680\cdot 10^{-12}}\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+10^{-5}\log\frac{10^{-5}}{1.17549\cdot 10^{-38}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 0.99999015168\cdot\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+0.00075823623," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.99999015168</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.00075823623</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 0.99999015168\cdot\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+0.00075823623,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">is accurate enough for limiting the true divergence to values on the order of <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 0.99999015168\cdot\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+0.00075823623" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.99999015168</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.00075823623</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 0.99999015168\cdot\textrm{KL}\left({p^{\prime}}\parallel{q^{\prime}}\right)+0.00075823623</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 0.99999015168\cdot 0.05+0.00075823623" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.99999015168</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.00075823623</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 0.99999015168\cdot 0.05+0.00075823623</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textrm{KL}\left({p}\parallel{q}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 0.050757743814." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.050757743814</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 0.050757743814.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Code</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While the theoretical derivation of the differentiable trust region projection looks convoluted, the final implementation is fairly straightforward.
We give PyTorch-adjacent pseudocode for the dense variant of the primal (<a href="#LST1" title="Listing 1 ‣ Appendix B Code ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and dual (<a href="#LST2" title="Listing 2 ‣ Appendix B Code ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) in the following.
Note that the sparse implementation mostly differs in the usage of a custom sparse tensor class that maintains a default probability for the implicit entries.
While this requires additional care in terms of indexing and allows for optimizations of, e.g., the <span title="Kullback-Leibler" class="ltx_glossaryref">KL</span> computation, the general logic remains unchanged.
<a href="#LST3" title="Listing 3 ‣ Appendix B Code ‣ TROLL: Trust Regions improve Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, shows our <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-ary bracketing method to optimize the dual.</p>
</div>
